    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Measure E is a countably additive measure; IsProbabilityMeasure means mass one. Kernel X Y is a measurable family of measures on Y indexed by X. IsMarkovKernel means every fiber has mass one.",
      "The right-associated product NNReal times E times Nat times (Nat to E) has its product measurable structure. For a state s, s.1 is a nonnegative real, s.2.1 an E element, s.2.2.1 a natural and s.2.2.2 an E-valued sequence. Nat.casesOn n y h equals y at zero and h(m) at n=m+1.",
      "mu.tilted(f) normalizes exp(f) against mu. GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing(P,r) is the actual law of X+rZ under P times the centered identity-covariance Gaussian; r is a standard-deviation scale.",
      "Measure.map is pushforward. Measure.bind applies a measure-valued function and integrates its event masses. Kernel composition L circle_k P first uses P and then L; P^0 is the identity kernel and P^(n+1) is n+1 successive uses.",
      "Finset.Iic k indexes natural numbers from zero to k. A product over Iic k is a finite path. Kernel.comap precomposes the input map; Kernel.map pushes forward the output. Kernel.partialTraj kappa 0 n is the iterated finite trajectory kernel that takes a path through time zero and appends coordinates through time n using kappa at each stage. The displayed last-coordinate projection and constant singleton input map are part of the statement."
